## 3. Why I stopped

The Red test's own `stringLeaves` helper flattens array elements as `presets[0].name`
(bracket notation). The pins of test 2 are looked up with `pin.path.join(".")`, so
`["presets","0","name"]` becomes the key `presets.0.name` (dot notation). With `presets` as the
array that spec 5.4 prints, the lookup misses and test 2 can never pass.

Spec section 5.4 prints `presets: [ ... ]` as an array literal, and spec section 5.3 pins the
component props as `presets: readonly { name: string; setup: string; result: string }[]`. Local
style agrees: `faq.items`, `valuePropositions.features`, `steps`, and `stats` are arrays in the
same dictionary file.

The only shape that passes test 2 is an object keyed `"0"`, `"1"`, `"2"`. That shape satisfies
all 18 tests, but it contradicts the spec's array contract and local style, and it would bake a
non-array `presets` into the dictionary that tasks 1.6 and 1.7 then pin.

Per the role contract, a committed Red test that contradicts the specification is immutable and
Green stops. I reverted the locale edit; the worktree is clean at 1a32da5b2 with no commit.

## 4. Question for the orchestrator

Retry Red (Mid Red retry) with one of:

1. Address the preset pins the way `stringLeaves` renders arrays: pin paths
   `["presets[0]", "name"]` and so on, or
2. Flatten arrays with dot indices inside `stringLeaves` so `presets.0.name` is the rendered
   key, or
3. Change the spec (5.3 and 5.4) to the object-keyed shape and let Green implement that shape.

Options 1 and 2 keep the spec's array. Green implements to whichever Red contract survives.

